RayCAD patch to OCCT 8.0.1 (LGPL-2.1 with the OCCT exception; this file is under the same terms).

What: ChFi3d_Builder::IntersectMoreCorner declares `int prol;` without a value and passes it to the static
ChFi3d_ExtendSurface(S, prol), whose first statement is `if (prol) return;` (prol is an in/out flag: "this surface is
already extended"). Initialise it to 0, as PerformOneCorner does for the same code. The same flag array in
PerformIntersectionAtEnd, prolface[], is set to 0 for indices 0 .. nbface-1 and nn, but the loop that intersects the
faces also calls ChFi3d_ExtendSurface(Sface, prolface[nb]) with nb == nbface; set that element to 0 too.

Why: the value read is whatever an earlier call left in that stack slot. When it is not 0, ChFi3d_ExtendSurface
returns at once and leaves prol set, so IntersectMoreCorner takes the "extended" branch with the face's own,
unextended surface: Bs is initialised on an unbounded copy of the face and DStr.SetNewSurface(Fv, Sface) is called
with the surface the face already has. If Fv lies on a periodic surface (a cylinder), TopOpeBRepBuild then rebuilds
it through TopOpeBRepDS_BuildTool::UpdateSurface (TopOpeBRepBuild_Builder::MakeFaces), which gives every edge of the
face one pcurve on the "new" surface: on the seam edge this replaces the pair of pcurves by one, the face is no
longer closed in U and BRepCheck reports it (UnorientableShape). Seen in RayCAD as a fillet or chamfer of a straight
edge ending at a vertex shared with a cylindrical pocket wall that failed in 1 to 2 % of the runs in one process
(depending on the heap and stack history of the process; forcing the flag to 0 gave the valid result every time,
forcing it to 1 gave the invalid solid every time). Where the slot happened to hold 0 the result was already right,
so nothing changes there.

Upstream: not fixed in OCCT master as of 2026-11-19 (`int prol;` and the missing prolface[nbface] are still there).
Not reported upstream yet.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
